<section class="section">
  <div class="shell split split--sticky">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Where we are</p>
      <h2>Roadmap</h2>
      <p>
        Written plainly, because a roadmap that only lists wins is not a roadmap.
      </p>
    </div>

    {#
      TODO: confirm the exact dates of the pilot and of the next milestone with the team
      before launch. Only the founding year is stated as a hard date here on purpose.
    #}
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline__when">{{ site.founded }}</span>
        <h3>Founded</h3>
        <p>
          Three students at the Zurich University of Applied Sciences start PATON after spending
          time on wards and watching how much of a shift the nurse call quietly consumes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline__when">Research</span>
        <h3>We went and counted</h3>
        <p>
          Observation and interviews on real wards, which is where the recurring pattern came from:
          request and qualification rarely line up, and the corridor gets walked twice.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline__when">Pilot</span>
        <h3>Geriatrische Klinik St.&nbsp;Gallen</h3>
        <p>
          The system runs on a live ward and logs more than a thousand call events, recording the
          qualification each request needed and the walking distance each response took.
          <a href="/case-study/">Read the case study.</a>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline__when">Now</span>
        <h3>Talking to wards</h3>
        <p>
          Working with clinics that want the same visibility, and turning the pilot's findings into
          a product that can be installed rather than accompanied.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

